    "abstract": "A low-level light sensor and preprocessor for a disposA/cm2 input optical able medical probe is described. A 10-Hz 4signal in the visible spectrum is assumed in chemoluminant diagnostic applications. A single-bit first-order sigma–delta modulator has been employed for analog-to-digital conversion, thanks to its robustness, simplicity, inherent linearity, and high signal-to-noise ratio. A current buffer has been used to replicate the weak signal with sufficient bandwidth. Tests have shown the feasibility of this approach, and have also enabled improvements of the design. Fig. 1. Smart sensor system.",
